Z||000000||fierospeeder||11-05-2000||02:48 AM||||im trying to figure out what are the two sensors on my moms car, 88 chevy celebrity wagon.  It has a 2.8 engine.<P>There are two sensors on the lower side of the block, opposite side of the starter.  <BR>There is one that has a small one inch long shaft with a large circle thing on it, and only one wire  going into it.  The other, sort of looks like a plastic figure 8 with two wires going into it and it is held down by a small 1/4"? bolt, and two wires are  coming out of that one.  <P>I having some oil coming out of someplace near those sensors, its not leaking but just making the block oily.  And the manuals i have dont really get into detail about the other sensors besides the oil pressure one.<P>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Terrybogin||11-05-2000||09:22 AM||||Hmmmm. Sounds like the knock sensor and the crank angle sensor.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||11-06-2000||07:48 AM||||Terry sounds correct! The only one that will produce an oil leak is the crank sensor, the knock sensor is a bottom hole.||||reg||1
